# Vercel Speed Insights Integration Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Sobus Innovent 2026 project following the latest official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added dependency**: `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0
- **Package manager**: npm (npm install was used as no existing lock file was present)
- **Updated files**: 
  - `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights to dependencies
  - `package-lock.json` - Created new lock file with dependency tree

### 2. Speed Insights Integration Script
- **Created file**: `js/speed-insights.js`
- **Implementation**: ES module that imports and calls `injectSpeedInsights()` from @vercel/speed-insights
- **Configuration**: Default settings with debug mode disabled for production
- **Documentation reference**: https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart

### 3. HTML Integration
- **Modified file**: `index.html`
- **Change**: Added `<script type="module" src="js/speed-insights.js"></script>` to the `<head>` section
- **Placement**: Right after the main stylesheet, before closing `</head>` tag
- **Script type**: ES module to support modern JavaScript imports

### 4. Git Configuration
- **Created file**: `.gitignore`
- **Purpose**: Exclude node_modules and other build artifacts from version control
- **Includes**: Standard patterns for Node.js projects (node_modules, build outputs, cache directories, etc.)

## Implementation Details

### Framework Detection
The project is a vanilla HTML/JavaScript website with no framework. It uses `npx serve` to run a local development server, as specified in the package.json scripts.

### Integration Method
Based on the latest Vercel documentation (fetched March 19, 2026), the implementation uses:
- The `@vercel/speed-insights` npm package
- ES module import from `@vercel/speed-insights/dist/index.mjs` (browser-compatible version)
- The `injectSpeedInsights()` function which automatically:
  - Initializes the Speed Insights tracking queue
  - Loads the Vercel tracking script from `/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js` when deployed
  - Tracks web vitals and performance metrics automatically

### How It Works
1. When the page loads, the browser executes `speed-insights.js` as an ES module
2. The module imports `injectSpeedInsights` from the installed package
3. `injectSpeedInsights()` creates a script element and appends it to the document head
4. The tracking script loads from Vercel's infrastructure (when deployed to Vercel)
5. Performance metrics are automatically collected and sent to Vercel Speed Insights

## Testing Performed
- ✅ Package installation completed successfully (npm install)
